---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { grantOfferById } from '../lib/grants';

const offer = grantOfferById.review;
const siteOrigin = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://www.wellridgegroup.com');
const siteURL = siteOrigin.toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const pageURL = `${siteURL}/grant-application-review`;
const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: offer.name,
  serviceType: 'Grant application review',
  areaServed: { '@type': 'Country', name: 'United States' },
  description: offer.description,
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Wellridge Group', url: siteURL },
  url: pageURL,
};
const offerSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Offer',
  name: offer.name,
  description: offer.description,
  price: offer.price.replace('$', ''),
  priceCurrency: 'USD',
  url: pageURL,
  itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: offer.name, url: pageURL },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nonprofit Grant Proposal Review & Editing Services"
  description={`${offer.price} nonprofit grant proposal review and editing, available nationwide. Up to 2,000 narrative words, tracked edits, and a missing-items checklist.`}
  structuredData={[serviceSchema, offerSchema]}
>
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-fog">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ridge-blue">Defined grant support</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-3 mb-6">Nonprofit grant proposal review and editing</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">When the words already exist, a focused review can show where the draft answers the funder, where facts or attachments are missing, and where the narrative and budget need to agree.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Available remotely to nonprofits throughout the United States. One existing foundation grant narrative, one review, and no recurring commitment.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ridge-blue">{offer.price} · {offer.payment} after scope agreement</p>
      <a href="/contact?service=grant-writing&package=review" class="inline-block mt-8 px-8 py-3 bg-ridge-blue text-white rounded-md text-lg font-medium">Discuss an application review</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-4">What this scope covers</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700">This is a review of one existing narrative, up to 2,000 words, against one controlling funder rubric or instruction set. The review follows the funder's questions and checks the internal story: population, activities, timing, outcomes, measures, request amount, and budget consistency.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">You receive tracked edits in the draft and a missing-items checklist that separates facts to confirm, attachments to locate, and approvals still needed. The work identifies gaps and proposes clear edits; it does not turn an assumption into an organizational fact.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 bg-fog">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ridge-blue">At a glance</p>
          <p class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mt-2">{offer.price} · {offer.payment}</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-4 text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1">
            {offer.deliverables.map((deliverable) => <li>{deliverable}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">{offer.timing}</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-4">What a grant narrative review looks like</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">This excerpt uses the fictional Northside Arts Workshop demonstration. The organization, numbers, and proposed activities are invented; this is not client work or an awarded grant.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border border-gray-200"><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-3">Before: a claim without a measure</h3><blockquote class="text-gray-700">“We expect the program to be successful and will evaluate it through attendance and feedback.”</blockquote></div>
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border border-well-green bg-green-50"><h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold mb-3">After: a specific planning target</h3><blockquote class="text-gray-700">“The planning target is for at least 18 of 24 enrolled students to attend five of six sessions.”</blockquote><p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">The revision names the target, denominator, and attendance threshold. A real review needs your approved targets; an editor cannot invent them.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mt-6">The accompanying checklist would flag the attendance-record owner, missing follow-up, and approval of the target. See the <a href="/work-examples/grant-review" class="text-ridge-blue underline">full annotated review and hypothetical budget</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-fog">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">Send only public fit information first</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700">For the initial inquiry, send the funder and program name, public instructions or URL, stated deadline and time zone, current draft length, and a short description of the approved program and budget. Include the name of the person who approves organizational facts.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">Do not put confidential client information, passwords, protected records, or sensitive attachments in the first inquiry. Once scope and access are agreed, we can arrange a separate secure handoff for the draft and approved materials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">A practical review process</h2>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Confirm the opportunity, rubric, scope, and secure materials handoff.</li>
            <li>Review the complete draft and approved source materials against the controlling instructions.</li>
            <li>Return tracked edits and the missing-items checklist within the stated timing after complete inputs and access.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">The client reviews the edits, confirms every fact, approves the final version, and submits it. Late or incomplete inputs move the working deadline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 bg-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">Fit and boundaries</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700">This scope fits an identified opportunity with a draft in hand. It includes one review; additional review rounds require a separate agreement. New program design, federal applications, complex budget creation, additional funders, portal administration, and submission are outside the package. The funder makes the award decision; Wellridge does not guarantee funding.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 text-gray-700">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-deep mb-3">Do you need editing or writing from scratch?</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">Choose this review when a complete narrative already exists and needs clearer answers, an instruction check, and identified gaps. If you have approved source materials but no draft, the <a href="/foundation-grant-writing" class="text-ridge-blue underline">one-time foundation application writing service</a> covers a different task. This package is nonprofit narrative support; it does not include scientific peer review or federal application review.</p>
        <p>See the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/work-examples/grant-review">fictional grant review example</a> for a demonstration of the format. Compare this scope with <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/letter-of-inquiry-writing">letter-of-inquiry writing</a>, all <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/grant-writing">grant-writing services</a>, <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/pricing#grant-pricing-questions">payment and scope answers</a>, or the <a class="text-ridge-blue underline" href="/resources/grant-review-loi-or-application">grant buyer guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
